    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-sch-2-sec-12",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "12 After subsection 301.6(1) of the Criminal Code",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus#sch-2-sec-12"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus.pdf, p.11",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(1A) However:\n\n(a) the regulations may provide that a listed border controlled\nprecursor is taken, for the purposes of this Part, to be a border\ncontrolled precursor only in relation to particular offences\nagainst this Part, or particular elements of those offences; and\n\n(b) if the regulations so provide, then the listed border controlled\nprecursor is taken, for the purposes of this Part, to be a border\ncontrolled precursor only in relation to those offences or\nelements.\n\n(1B) To avoid doubt, if a listed border controlled precursor is taken, for\nthe purposes of this Part, to be a border controlled precursor only\nin relation to particular offences against this Part, or particular\nelements of those offences, then a salt, ester or immediate\nprecursor of the listed border controlled precursor is taken, for the\npurposes of this Part, to be a border controlled precursor only in\nrelation to those offences or elements.\n\nSchedule 2  Border controlled drugs, plants and precursors\n\nCrimes and Other Legislation Amendment (Omnibus No. 2) Act 2023\nNo. 98, 2023\n\nDefinition of immediate precursor",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\n\n(1A) However:\n\n(a) the regulations may provide that a listed border controlled\nprecursor is taken, for the purposes of this Part, to be a border\ncontrolled precursor only in relation to particular offences\nagainst this Part, or particular elements of those offences; and\n\n(b) if the regulations so provide, then the listed border controlled\nprecursor is taken, for the purposes of this Part, to be a border\ncontrolled precursor only in relation to those offences or\nelements.\n\n(1B) To avoid doubt, if a listed border controlled precursor is taken, for\nthe purposes of this Part, to be a border controlled precursor only\nin relation to particular offences against this Part, or particular\nelements of those offences, then a salt, ester or immediate\nprecursor of the listed border controlled precursor is taken, for the\npurposes of this Part, to be a border controlled precursor only in\nrelation to those offences or elements.\n\nSchedule 2  Border controlled drugs, plants and precursors\n\nCrimes and Other Legislation Amendment (Omnibus No. 2) Act 2023\nNo. 98, 2023\n\nDefinition of immediate precursor",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-sch-2-sec-12-ss-1a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus-sch-2-sec-12-ss-1b"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8445d5cfe714f4491bdd7be3a32948e53e2a96ef2d6d75ca8d501fbc73a359c4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus#sch-2-sec-12",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "12 After subsection 301.6(1) of the Criminal Code",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 11,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(1A) However:\n\n(a) the regulations may provide that a listed border controlled\nprecursor is taken, for the purposes of this Part, to be a border\ncontrolled precursor only in relation to particular offences\nagainst this Part, or particular elements of those offences; and\n\n(b) if the regulations so provide, then the listed border controlled\nprecursor is taken, for the purposes of this Part, to be a border\ncontrolled precursor only in relation to those offences or\nelements.\n\n(1B) To avoid doubt, if a listed border controlled precursor is taken, for\nthe purposes of this Part, to be a border controlled precursor only\nin relation to particular offences against this Part, or particular\nelements of those offences, then a salt, ester or immediate\nprecursor of the listed border controlled precursor is taken, for the\npurposes of this Part, to be a border controlled precursor only in\nrelation to those offences or elements.\n\nSchedule 2  Border controlled drugs, plants and precursors\n\nCrimes and Other Legislation Amendment (Omnibus No. 2) Act 2023\nNo. 98, 2023\n\nDefinition of immediate precursor"
    },
