      "dc:source": "crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-omnibus.pdf, p.13",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(1) Subsection (2) applies if a substance or plant is a border controlled\ndrug or a border controlled plant because of a determination made\nunder section 301.13 of the Criminal Code (which deals with\nemergency Ministerial determinations of serious drugs).\nNote:\nBorder controlled drug and border controlled plant have the same\nmeaning as in Part 9.1 of the Criminal Code (see subsection 4(1) of\nthis Act). In that Part, those terms include substances or plants that\n\nSchedule 2  Border controlled drugs, plants and precursors\n\nCrimes and Other Legislation Amendment (Omnibus No. 2) Act 2023\nNo. 98, 2023\n\nare, under section 301.13 of the Criminal Code, taken, for the\npurposes of the Part, to be border controlled drugs or border controlled\nplants only in relation to particular offences against the Part, or\nparticular elements of those offences.",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(1) Subsection (2) applies if a substance or plant is a border controlled\ndrug or a border controlled plant because of a determination made\nunder section 301.13 of the Criminal Code (which deals with\nemergency Ministerial determinations of serious drugs).\nNote:\nBorder controlled drug and border controlled plant have the same\nmeaning as in Part 9.1 of the Criminal Code (see subsection 4(1) of\nthis Act). In that Part, those terms include substances or plants that\n\nSchedule 2  Border controlled drugs, plants and precursors\n\nCrimes and Other Legislation Amendment (Omnibus No. 2) Act 2023\nNo. 98, 2023\n\nare, under section 301.13 of the Criminal Code, taken, for the\npurposes of the Part, to be border controlled drugs or border controlled\nplants only in relation to particular offences against the Part, or\nparticular elements of those offences.",
      "cml:asserts": [
